well it's about time Apple it only took  you 14 versions to catch up but you  finally did it  what's going on guys my name's Dave  atomic welcome back to the channel today  we're talking about the brand new  version of iPad OS 14 OS 14 and  absolutely everything to do with the  WWDC 2020 if you're new to the tech  space and first of all have no idea what  WWDC 2020 stands for it stands for the  Worldwide Developers Conference in 2020  this is an Apple hosted event that was  for the first time ever hosted over the  worldwide Internet usually it is a  face-to-face conference with tickets  costing upwards of fifteen hundred US  dollars however because of the whole  kovin 19 pandemic Apple is opted for the  online only experience absolutely free  of charge so this time around we've had  hundreds and hundreds of developers and  tech fanatics like myself be able to  tune in to the WWDC and experience  absolutely everything there for example  right now I have the iPad OS 14 up and  running on a 6th gen iPad in front of me  the 6th gen iPad is able to run OS 14  without a problem on the list every  single device that is expected to be  able to run iOS 14 when it launches  officially later in September or October  this year right now the version running  on my iPad is the developers beta the  developers beta is available for all  individuals who wish to pay the  developers beta costs of I believe it is  99 US dollars or you can find yourself a  free developers beta at the link below  now just quickly I have no affiliation  to this site it is just where I managed  to find my developers beta to download  and utilize for the purposes of this  video now I've spent the last day  playing around with iOS 14 and all  new features and functions that are  available to this device obviously  everything on an iPad is slightly  different to what is available on an  iPhone there are some key differences  but overall is predominantly the same  let's start with the biggest and most  talked-about feature and that is the  widgets on the side panel so if you're  an iPad user unfortunately right now in  the beta's developers version you can  only have the widgets in the today  section of the menu which permanently is  not on the screen you cannot drag and  drop these widgets onto the homescreen  into positions like you can on the  iPhone now this is something that I'm  hoping will change in the future because  it would be nice to have these widgets  on your home screen on an iPad  especially with that much much larger  real estate however at the time being as  this is recorded which is let me just  check the date the 28th of June at 8:33  p.m. there is no implementation of the  widgets onto the home screen on the iPad  OS what it does have on the other hand  is the same three widget system that the  iPhone has it features a small medium  and a large widget for a selected  variety of apps at the moment there  isn't too many available on the iPad  that is predominantly for the fact that  it's brand-new just released but more  and more developers will come to the  party at the moment Apple has noted in  their developing guidelines that the  small widget which is actually most of  my widgets on this iPad if I'm being  honest this is technically considered a  small widget when you tap on it it  automatically opens up the app it does  not open up as a button or as a feature  so for example if I were to scroll down  here to the larger widget which gives me  more information about my activity on  this iPad and you just tap on Safari or  whatever it opens it directly to that  feature something that has changed the  predominant way an iPhone user use  their iPhone is the app library now the  app library is an automatic accumulation  of all your apps grouped together by  what I'm assuming is an algorithm and  automatically distributed into different  folders for your convenience  it is usually located at the very end of  your pages which now you can also hide  but we'll get to that in a second  unfortunately with the iPad OS there is  no app library so it doesn't matter how  far we swipe across there is absolutely  no app library this is a bit of a  letdown considering that more people  would have larger storage space on their  iPad more apps more games more diversity  in what they have and it would be a nice  little additional feature maybe we will  see this in the full release maybe right  but for the time being it is not in the  iPad OS another thing that isn't  available on the iPad but it is  available on iPhone OS is the simple  fact that you can hide pages from your  view so usually if you're an iPhone user  or you have anything like me you have a  ton of apps sitting in a random folder  or a ton of apps sitting on another page  hidden at the back of your iPhone now  you can actually go into what Apple has  claimed it jiggle mode I just go into  jiggle mode and automatically activate  and deactivate different pages of your  iPhone so if you have 10 pages to scroll  through to get to the back one you can  now just hide all nine of them so you  only have your main pages that you need  and switch to the app library when you  need it now obviously if you're an  Android user this has been a thing for  decades and it's nothing new it is how  we operate it is how the system has been  designed but having said that Apple has  done this in their own unique little way  Android has had widgets time and time  again  whereas iPhone and  has now introduced the stacked widgets  so stacked widgets is a very Apple way  of developing in a very Apple way of  creating a new feature so stacking  widgets allows you to literally do that  stack your favorite widgets one on top  of the other in order to create your  favorite stack and then you can quickly  just swipe through them to get all the  notifications you need that way you  don't take up all the real estate and  you get all the functionality of it  something I'd definitely like to see on  an Android but for now I'm happy that  it's on the iPad now another feature  that's unique to the iPad is an update  to the Apple pencil if you're a user  like me who uses the Apple pencil all  the time and you have a tendency to  write text more than you have to type so  for me personally I'm usually in a  meeting taking notes this is the easiest  and quickest way for me to take notes  without really disrupting the meeting  and acting in a professional manner for  me it's just write notes keep talking  and keep conducting the meeting whereas  if I were typing constantly I'd be  looking down shifting changing and it'd  be a little bit more inappropriate a  good thing that has come to Apple iPad  OS 14 now is scribble-scribble allows  you to write like you normally would  with a pencil but it automatically  translates that into text I've been  having a good go at this for a solid two  hours as I was scribbling different  things to see how it would work and  honestly it's pretty good my handwriting  is not the best but it is able to  capture most of what I write if I take a  little bit of time to slow down and  articulate my words properly then it  definitely captures almost every single  word I wrote the good thing is if you're  an artist or just somebody having a play  with shapes and features if you start  drawing a shape and pause just before  you finish it it'll automatically detect  that shape and create the perfect shape  for you  so for example I'm right-handed but to  draw a perfect circle with my left hand  is now  very easy so a very simple feature that  should have been introduced a long time  ago but as technology improves obviously  so do the things that go with it  this is a feature I'm very excited to  continue using and look forward to  seeing in the full release of iOS 14 now  if you haven't really understood the  theme so far it's a whole refresh of the  UI the UI has gotten a lot sleeker a lot  more compact a lot more elegant and in  my opinion a lot more Apple there's been  a redesign from the iPad to the iWatch 2  TV system all the way through the larger  updates of their operating system of  their Mac books and Mac computers so  what you'll notice now is if you get a  call for example it used to take up your  whole iPhone screen now instead there'll  only be a little bit of a drop down from  the top that you can swipe away or  answer depending on what you want to do  with that call which doesn't disrupt  your complete workflow the same thing  goes with Siri Siri used to open up and  dominate your entire screen whereas now  if we just go hey Siri it's a little bit  slow but it only opens up in the bottom  corner what you will also notice is up  in the top a little orange icon appears  next to the Wi-Fi symbol on the iPad now  what that means is the fact that the  microphone is active if that orange  light were to go green for example it  means an application is using your  camera so this is a great way to manage  the privacy on your device if something  is using your microphone or your camera  in the background that you aren't aware  of it is very very simple to understand  now that something is using it even  though Siri has gotten a more compact  much more minimalistic appearance  unfortunately it isn't utilizable in a  multitasking way so  Siri is in the bottom corner or only  taking up a tiny portion of your iPhone  screen you'd think that you'd be able to  use the  ground apps and continue scrolling at  your Safari page for example well note  unfortunately once you tap away from  Syria or try to scroll it completely  remove Siri and gets on with the app  you're using before something that can  be used simultaneously is  picture-in-picture mode something that  has been around on an android for  decades but we won't get into that  picture-in-picture mode now allows you  to for example if you're watching a full  screen video get out of that video going  to your notes type a quick note come  back to that video or if you're in  FaceTime get out of FaceTime find the  phone number and then tell them that  phone number directly in a smaller  picture and picture you can resize move  from one corner to another anywhere in  the screen that you like whereas  previously it would close out of that  app open another app pause your FaceTime  Rives resume the FaceTime later on and  it would just be a nightmare so now it's  definitely a much easier much more  native picture-in-picture mode that is a  great addition to iOS 14 something that  hasn't been spoken about iOS 14 too  often on YouTube is the integration of  iOS 14 and air pods this is actually  something really cool and something I am  definitely jealous of as an Android user  yes Android has this but not as good so  with the new air pods you're going to  have the ability of smart switching now  what this means is that the Bluetooth in  your ear pods and the connectivity  between your Apple devices all talk to  each other so if you're sitting there  watching something on your iPad with  your ear pods in you put your iPad down  you go over there you grab up your  iPhone and you start doing another video  on your iPhone your ear pods will  automatically switch to that iPhone  audio instead of the iPad audio you had  going on before this also works if  you're on your iPhone and then switch to  your macbook and vice versa this is  something that makes transitioning your  Bluetooth headphones so so easy it is  definitely definitely a useful feature  and something that you realize is  incredible without  realizing it another little feature that  has changed slightly but it is quite  noticeable if you're paying attention to  detail the new update has increased the  saturation and brightness of your device  so your blacks have gotten richer and  darker and your whites have gotten  crisper all your colors have become more  vibrant and cleaner it isn't something  that you're going to notice unless you  pay attention  for example the Notes app the black is  now truly black it isn't a dulled out  gray anymore so this is just a simple  change but again it is moving into that  new style that new Apple way and that  new Apple branding one downside of the  beta version of iOS 14 though is the  fact that it is actually chewing my  battery a little bit quicker than I like  it too I don't know if it's just the  beta if it's some bugs early on but it  is definitely going through the battery  in about an hour and a half I've lost  about 30% so an iPad not so great  usually I'd get maybe about 30% more  than that  so it isn't terrible but it is  noticeable anyway that's all I've had  the liberty of playing around with on  iPad OS 14 and iOS 14 if you have any  questions about the software how to  install it how to find out all the extra  features or really something more  specific about the software feel free to  leave a comment down below I reply to as  many people as I can thank you so much  for watching I truly do hope you enjoyed  the video if you did make sure you smash  that subscribe button  20:20 style and as always I see you next  Monday

